# LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default. The bench corpus is
# verified by SHA-256 against its manifest, rule fixtures and scanner tests compare
# exact bytes, and shell scripts must not carry `\r` — so on Windows the corpus hash
# check failed before any code ran. Text is normalized to LF instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
